  "version": 1,
  "notes": "Race rules per vehicle class, keyed by the class id in vehicles.json; a class missing here gets generic defaults. Percentages are shares of the lap time. field: default grid size, cars per team and the spread (standard deviation) of car and driver pace. race: default length, either distanceKm (laps rounded up) or minutes, and a time limit. pace: racePct is how much slower race laps are than qualifying before fuel and tyres (engine modes, tyre saving); consistencyPct the lap-to-lap scatter; overtaking scales how easily passes succeed. fuel: typical kg per km on the reference circuits, tank size, refuelling rate (0 = no refuelling). tyres: compounds with their pace offset to the fastest, life in km on the reference circuits and pace lost at the end of that life; mustUseTwo requires two different compounds in a race. pit: whether stops are allowed at all, stationary time for four tyres, whether refuelling and tyres happen at once, mandatory stops and the shortest stationary time of a mandatory stop. drs: the lap from which it is enabled and the gap in seconds at the detection point. air: share of drag removed when right behind another car, and share of downforce lost in its wake. incidents: chances per lap and technical retirements per 1000 km. reference: average wheel energy (MJ/km) and tyre work per km on the real circuits in data/circuits, printed by scripts/raceReference.ts; fuel and tyre wear scale with a track's own values against these. All figures are approximate defaults meant to be edited.",
